# Copy to .env.local for local development:  cp .env.example .env.local
# .env.local is gitignored; .env.example (this file) is committed.

# Base URL of the Thrift Vault backend API.
#
# This is the ONLY place the backend URL is configured. src/lib/api.js appends
# bare routes to it ("/auth/login", "/products/<id>", ...), and the backend mounts
# its router at /api/v1 — so this value MUST include the /api/v1 suffix and MUST
# NOT have a trailing slash. Getting that wrong produces 404s on every request.
#
#   correct:   https://thrift-vault-api.fly.dev/api/v1
#   wrong:     https://thrift-vault-api.fly.dev            (missing /api/v1)
#   wrong:     https://thrift-vault-api.fly.dev/api/v1/    (trailing slash)
#
# Local development (backend running via `npm run dev` on port 4000):
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api/v1
#
# Vercel production — set this in Project Settings > Environment Variables, for
# the Production (and Preview) environments:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://thrift-vault-api.fly.dev/api/v1
#
# Vite inlines this value at BUILD time, not at runtime. Changing it in Vercel
# does nothing until you redeploy.
